 "drivingQuestion": "How does one ask for meat on a Festival without naming a price?",
 "outcome": "resolved",
 "outcomeNote": "local portion names avoid mention of price",
 "continuesQuestionOf": null,
 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "beitzah.28b.16",
   "daf": "28b",
   "sentenceId": 15,
   "he": "גְּמָ׳ הֵיכִי עָבֵיד? כִּי הָא",
   "en": "«GEMARA:» The Gemara asks: «What» should one «do» if he wishes to take part of an animal on a Festival, but is barred from mentioning its price? The Gemara answers: «As»"
  },
  {
   "id": "beitzah.29a.1",
   "daf": "29a",
   "sentenceId": 0,
   "he": "דִּבְסוּרָא אָמְרִי: תַּרְטָא וּפַלְגוּ תַּרְטָא. בְּנַרֶשׁ אָמְרִי: חֶלְקָא וּפַלְגוּ חֶלְקָא. בְּפוּמְבְּדִיתָא אָמְרִי: אוּזְיָא וּפַלְגוּ אוּזְיָא. בִּנְהַר פְּקוֹד וּבְמָתָא מַחְסֵיָא אָמְרִי: רִבְעָא וּפַלְגוּ רִבְעָא.",
   "en": "«they would say in Sura:» Give me that cut of meat called «a tarta or half a tarta,» without naming a price. «In Neresh they would say» in reference to those same portions: «A part or half a part. In Pumbedita they would say: An uzya or half an uzya. In Nehar Pekod and in Mata Meḥasya they would say:» Give me «a quarter or half a quarter,» thereby establishing the size of the portion without mentioning its price."
  }
 ],
